+# MCP client checkup
+
+Checked `http://127.0.0.1:52028/mcp` locally on 2026-10-18, without authorization. The server was started from `server.py` and stopped after the checks. Only the two tools advertised with `readOnlyHint: true` were called. The server is not listed in a registry, according to `README.md`.
+
+| Check | Result | Evidence | Story for failure |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| C1 · Anonymous tool list and discovery | PASS | `initialize` HTTP 200 with a result; `tools/list` HTTP 200 with 3 tools. `server/discover` HTTP 200, JSON-RPC `-32601` (method not found), which the guide accepts. | — |
+| C2 · Tool refusals | FAIL | `get_note` with `n-999999`: HTTP 200, JSON-RPC error `-32602`, `note not found: n-999999`. Missing `id`: HTTP 200, JSON-RPC error `-32602`, `missing required argument: id`. Neither has a result with `isError: true`. | [A real client threw where my test passed](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-10-02-my-live-mcp-test-asserted-the-bug-a-real-client-threw-where-) |
+| C3 · Session after error | PASS | The same `Mcp-Session-Id` was returned and sent on the next request. After both C2 errors, `get_note(id=n-1)` returned HTTP 200 with a normal result and `isError: false`. | — |
+| C4 · Published output schemas | PASS | Both read-only tools with `outputSchema` returned HTTP 200, `isError: false`, and `structuredContent`. `get_note(n-1)` has the required `id`, `title`, `body`, and integer `words`; `search_notes(query=soil)` returned an object, satisfying its published `{"type":"object"}` schema. | — |
+| C5 · Serialization and result agreement | FAIL | All observed bodies parsed as JSON, but `search_notes(query=soil)` returned `content[0].text` as a JSON **array** of hits while `structuredContent` was an **object** with `hits` and `total`. They do not agree. `get_note` text and structured content agreed. | [My tests passed because they agreed with me](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-28-my-tests-passed-because-they-agreed-with-me) |
+| C6 · Version and surface lock | FAIL | `initialize` reports `notes-mcp` version `0.3.1`. `README.md` says there is no registry listing; the tracked files are only `README.md`, `server.py`, and `notes.json`. No committed surface fingerprint or test locks the advertised schemas and capabilities to that version. The source shows a fixed resource list, although anonymous `resources/list` and `resources/templates/list` each return HTTP 401 despite advertised resource capability. Registry comparison and an independent fingerprint verdict are unavailable without a registry entry. | [My listing said read-only. My server could write.](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-30-my-mcp-listing-said-read-only-my-server-could-write) |
+| C7 · Per-call logs | FAIL | Individual calls produced structured stderr records with `method`, `tool`, `ok`, `ms`, and `who`, including errors. But `server.py`'s `do_POST` batch branch returns before `log(...)`; JSON-RPC calls sent in a batch therefore produce no per-call records. This is a source finding; no batch request was sent. | [Getting per-tool, per-user analytics](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-23-your-mcp-server-is-one-url-getting-per-tool-per-user-analyti) |
+| C8 · Tool count and names | PASS | `tools/list` HTTP 200: 3 names, `search_notes`, `get_note`, `add_note`. All match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`. `add_note` was not called. | — |
+| C9 · Version negotiation | PASS | `initialize` with `protocolVersion: "banana"` returned HTTP 200 and `protocolVersion: "2025-06-18"`; it did not echo `banana`. | — |
+| C10 · Wrong-answer rejection | FAIL | `search_notes` publishes only `{"type":"object"}`. A corrupted object such as `{"hits":"mcp-drill-corruption","total":-999999999}` satisfies that schema: it has no properties, required fields, or value constraints to reject it. `get_note` has constraints such as the `id` pattern and `words` minimum. No JSON Schema validator was installed locally, so this conclusion follows directly from the published `search_notes` schema rather than a validator run. | [My MCP server's output schemas accepted wrong answers](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-10-15-my-mcp-server-s-output-schemas-accepted-wrong-answers-7-of-8) |
+
+**has the problem**
+
+Unavailable checks: the Registry version comparison and independent fingerprint verification need a published registry name/version and fingerprint; a full C10 validator run needs a JSON Schema validator. C2–C5 were exercised without a token. No write tool was called, no token was used or printed, and no result was sent to an external service.
